      "title": "SHORT DEPENDENCIES ARE REDUNDANCY CERTIFICATES, NOT INFORMATION: define relation-generation entropy as H_k = log2 of the number of logarithm vectors consistent with the first k relations, measure bits per decomposition attempt on the same streams as IDEA-20260905-029c9c, and derive at zero compute that (E1) a vector of the dependency lattice L_K, however short, can only certify that a row added zero bits, while (E2) every zero-cost bit comes from a free relation in the row lattice L_R, whose count is the known automorphism/negation quotient -- so an anomalously short L_K cannot lower relation-collection cost, and the conditional ceiling on any L_R anomaly is a constant factor <= |Aut(E)|",
